My name is Fábio José. Hello.

I am a guy living in São Paulo, BR, with my wife and my dog.

I work as a researcher in Computer Engineering, mostly applied Machine Learning. I teach, too, and it's my favourite part of my job.
Probably the key thing about me is that I have many different interests. That's cool for talking about the unexpected and important intersections between them, and it's difficult to explain in grant applications. Academia likes their specialists.

I have been interested in sharing my thoughts about our relationships with technology, and art, and communities. To be honest I couldn't be precise as to what I want to write about since I'm still new to this and I enjoy the chaotic process of letting creativity take the wheel.

To mention some of those many interests, Music has always played a big role in my life, and I concern myself a lot with Political Theory, which pushes me towards learning History, Economics, and so on. I'm pretty keen on learning languages, too. The programming and the speaking kind.

If you're reading this, I encourage you to reach out. There is a silent community waiting to come together just under the surface of these online corners. You can reach me by e-mail as fabiozeh at the domain that hosts this page.
